From bd0f4d21261e3f07c5dfd10dd0e389ca8d756c1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alg Ore <hyperionxxx@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:40:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Update Express and consolidate the dashboard API installation

---
 README.md                         |   6 +
 api-server/package-lock.json      | 374 ---------------------
 api-server/package.json           |  15 -
 docs/api-dependency-upgrade.md    | 102 ++++++
 docs/runtime-dependency-review.md |  66 ++--
 docs/snapshot-storage.md          |  29 ++
 package-lock.json                 | 527 ++++++++++++++++++------------
 package.json                      |   5 +-
 8 files changed, 476 insertions(+), 648 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 api-server/package-lock.json
 delete mode 100644 api-server/package.json
 create mode 100644 docs/api-dependency-upgrade.md

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8a63754..f1fb5d7 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ collector WebSocket check. Install dependencies from the existing lock with
 `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund` for these local checks; this does
 not constitute a dependency advisory review or production runtime selection.
 
+The API uses the same root backend installation. Follow the
+[API install/start instructions](docs/snapshot-storage.md#install-and-start)
+and [dependency acceptance](docs/api-dependency-upgrade.md). Start it with
+`npm run start:api` from the repository root after supplying its required
+service settings.
+
 The pinned PostgreSQL driver has [real database validation](docs/postgres-validation.md).
 That optional suite requires a disposable cluster. The separate
 `npm run test:persistence` suite tests snapshot ingestion and the read API. Database processes now also require `DB_TIMEOUT_MS`.
