 response reached the writer. This is dashboard observation data, not chain
 finality or a claim that every node recently sent a report.
 
+## Install and start
+
+Use a fresh release directory with the selected Node/npm runtime. From the
+repository root, install the shared backend lock:
+
+```sh
+npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund
+```
+
+The API has no separate package manifest, lock or dependency installation.
+Do not carry `api-server/node_modules` over from an older release: nested
+packages would shadow the tested root packages. The frontend build remains
+separate. See [API dependency acceptance](api-dependency-upgrade.md) for the
+tested package/runtime and remaining release requirements.
+
+After provisioning the schema and supplying the required API/DB/freshness
+settings through the protected service environment, start the API from the
+repository root:
+
+```sh
+npm run start:api
+```
+
+The equivalent explicit service command is `node api-server/server.js`, with
+the release root as its working directory. Update older service definitions
+that ran `npm start` inside `api-server`; `npm start` now selects the root
+collector command. Service supervision and graceful lifecycle acceptance
+remain separate launch work.
+
 ## Provisioning
 
 Create a separate database and service roles through your normal PostgreSQL
